                <pb facs="0259" n="1219" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1219"/>

                <head>No. 801.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bragg to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 23, 1888</date>.
                        (Received July 31.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under your instruction No. 87, of the 11th
                    instant, I have made formal request of Mr. Mariscal to cause orders to be issued
                    (pending application for their extradition) for the arrest of Gulie Shields and
                    Isaac Wilson, charged with murder.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwd. S. Bragg.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
